    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About these metrics",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 41
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Two kinds of freshness\n\nThe **Freshness** stat panels above measure `time() - last_success_timestamp` — how long since the exporter last **successfully polled** each provider. Green ≤ 10 min, Yellow ≤ 30 min, Red beyond. A green panel means the exporter is collecting data normally.\n\n**A green freshness panel does not mean cost data is current.** Provider billing-history APIs have their own publication lag, independent of the exporter’s poll interval:\n\n| Provider | Token data | Cost data |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenAI | Within minutes | ~1–2 hours |\n| Azure OpenAI | Within minutes | **24–72 hours** |\n| Anthropic | Within minutes | ~1–4 hours |\n| Google Gemini | Within minutes | **1–2 days** |\n| AWS Bedrock | Within minutes | **24–48 hours** |\n\nUse token-rate panels (see the Tokens & Caching dashboard) as the near-real-time spend signal. Budget alerts fired from `llm_usage_cost_usd_total` reflect data already delayed by the amounts above.\n\n---\n\n**Poll success / failure** is incremented once per polling iteration per (tenant, provider) registration. A credential failure on one provider does not stop the others.\n\n**Last poll duration** captures wall-clock time for that provider’s `GetUsageAsync` + `GetCostsAsync` pair.\n\n---\n\n## OTLP pipeline panels\n\n**OTLP exporter errors** and **queue utilization** panels query the OTel collector’s self-metrics (exposed on port 8888 by default). Add a Prometheus scrape job for `otelcol:8888` to populate these panels — they show `No data` until the collector’s own metrics are scraped.\n\nIf OTLP fails, Prometheus exposition continues independently. A non-zero error rate means the OTLP signal surface is degraded; the Prometheus counters in the rows above remain authoritative.\n\n**See also:** [docs/failure-modes.md](https://github.com/your-org/llm-usage-exporter/blob/main/docs/failure-modes.md)"
      }
    }
  ]
}